Assembler Version 17
====================
Assembled by: version 16 debug build (asm_debug.out with define:enable_debug)

Build notes: The v16 debug build is used because v17 source uses
.ifdef enable_debug conditional compilation. Version 17 is self-hosting:
it can assemble its own source code, verified by diff of asm.out vs
asm_2.out (and asm_debug.out vs asm_debug_2.out).

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 16, plus .ifndef, .else, directive hash table
dispatch, enhanced conditional assembly, and major source refactoring:

Syntax:
- Standard 6502 mnemonic syntax (LDA, STA, etc.)
- All addressing modes (immediate, zero page, absolute, indexed, indirect)
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Decimal constants
- Character literals: 'x', '\n', '\\', '\''
- Expression evaluation with +, -, <<, >> operators (left-to-right)
- Quoted strings with full escape sequence support
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment
- Optional colon after label definitions (label:)
- Local labels with . prefix
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly with forward reference tracking
- Automatic zero page vs absolute addressing

Directives:
- .include filename - includes contents of another file
- .zeropage - switch to zero page section
- .code - switch to code section
- .byte expr [, expr ...] - emit byte values (comma-separated)
- .word expr [, expr ...] - emit 16-bit word values (comma-separated)
- .asciiz expr [, "string" ...] - emit null-terminated strings/values
- .reserve N - reserve N bytes (zero-fill in .code, PC advance in .zeropage)
- .byte / .word (without operand in .zeropage) - allocate zero page storage
- .ifdef label - begin conditional block if label is defined
- .ifndef label - begin conditional block if label is NOT defined (new)
- .else - alternative branch in conditional block (new)
- .endif - end conditional block
- .macro NAME [param1, param2, ...] - begin macro definition
- .endmacro - end macro definition

Conditional assembly:
- .ifdef/.ifndef/.else/.endif with up to 16 levels of nesting
- IFDEF_DECISIONS buffer for deterministic pass 2 replay
- ELSE_SEEN_ARRAY tracks duplicate .else per nesting level
- COND_INVERT mechanism shares logic between .ifdef and .ifndef

Macro system:
- Macro definitions stored on heap with body text and parameter names
- Invocation by macro name (parsed like instructions)
- Text substitution of parameters during expansion
- Local labels (.label) scoped per invocation via EXPANSION_ID
- Parameters live as activation slots on the macro's source-stack frame
  (resolved by ss_lookup_param_slot before falling through to the global
  hash); no per-invocation hash entries
- Recursion detection by walking the source-stack chain
  (ss_walk_frames_by_type filtering memory frames)

Command line:
- Variable argument count
- define:label - pre-define a label
- debug - enable debug output (debug build only)
- small_heap - use reduced heap for testing (debug build only)
- show_captured_macros - display macro definitions (debug build only)

Memory protection:
- Heap/stack collision detection with 256-byte safety buffer

Error handling: same categories as version 16, plus:
- err_else_without_ifdef (22): .else outside conditional block
- err_duplicate_else (23): Multiple .else in same block
- err_conditional_nesting_too_deep (24): Exceeds 16 nesting levels
- err_comma_expected (40): Missing comma in data directive
- err_asciiz_in_zeropage (41): .asciiz not allowed in .zeropage section
- Error messages use .asciiz format with decimal error codes

New in this version (relative to version 16):
- .ifndef directive (inverse of .ifdef)
  - COND_INVERT variable: $00 for ifdef (skip if not found),
    $FF for ifndef (assemble if not found)
  - process_conditional_common shared between dir_ifdef and dir_ifndef
- .else directive for conditional blocks
  - dir_else toggles skip state at current nesting depth
  - ELSE_SEEN_ARRAY at $0680 tracks whether .else has been used
    at each nesting depth (prevents duplicate .else)
- Conditional nesting limit of 16 levels (err_conditional_nesting_too_deep)
- Directive dispatch via instruction hash table (MODE_DIRECTIVE)
  - Directives looked up using same hash table as instructions
  - JUMP_TARGET16 and do_jump for indirect directive dispatch
  - process_conditional_directive checks for all 4 conditional directives
- .data directive removed (replaced by .byte/.word/.asciiz)
- Error messages use .asciiz with comma-separated decimal error code
  and string (e.g., .asciiz 1, "Label not found")
- Major source refactoring into many modules:
  - directives.asm: directive dispatch, data directives, conditional assembly
  - expressions.asm: expression evaluation
  - instructions.asm: instruction encoding and emission
  - labels.asm: label capture and lookup
  - output.asm: code emission and PC management
  - tokenizer.asm: token reading, filename reading, escape decoding
  - macro_capture.asm: macro definition capture
  - macro_expansion.asm: macro invocation and expansion
  - forward_ref.asm: forward reference tracking (renamed from fwdref.asm)
  - init.asm: initialization, argument parsing, input/output setup
  - instruction_tables.asm: instruction and addressing mode tables
- asm.asm reduced to ~338 lines (memory layout, includes, assembly loop,
  entry point, reset/interrupt vectors)

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
- Standard 6502 mnemonic syntax
- All addressing modes including indirect indexed
- .byte directive for zero page allocation (operand-less form)
- .word directive for zero page allocation (operand-less form)
- .byte with values (e.g., .byte 0 for BRK success code)
- .word with label values (e.g., .word start for reset vector)
- .asciiz for null-terminated strings (e.g., .asciiz "Heap used: ")
- .asciiz with comma-separated values (e.g., .asciiz 1, "Label not found")
- Hex constants ($xx and $xxxx)
- Decimal constants (e.g., .asciiz 1, .asciiz 240)
- Character literals and character literal expressions
- Expressions with +, -, <<, >> operators
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Labels with colon suffix (label:)
- Label assignments (e.g., OPERAND16 = HEX16)
- Local labels with . prefix
- PC setting (* = $2000 and * = $FFFC)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Comments (;)
- BRK with inline data via .asciiz
- .include directive (17 source modules)
- .zeropage and .code directives
- .ifdef enable_debug / .endif conditional compilation
- Macro definitions (.macro / .endmacro) in macros.asm
- Macro invocations (INC16, DEC16, SET16, CP16, CMP16, CMPI16, TST16,
  ADC16, ADCI16, ADCA16, SBC16, SBCI16, ASL16, LSR16, ROL16, ROR16,
  STA_LH16, PUSH16, POP16, LDAX16, STAX16, CHECK_FOR_OUT_OF_MEMORY,
  SHOW_MESSAGEI, SHOW_MESSAGE, SHOW_CHAR)

New syntax used in source (relative to version 16):
- .byte directive (replaces .data $00 for zero page allocation and byte data)
- .word directive (replaces .data $0000 for zero page allocation and word data)
- .asciiz directive for null-terminated strings
- .asciiz with comma-separated values (e.g., .asciiz 1, "message")
- Decimal constants (e.g., in .asciiz error data)

Other source changes:
- Source split into 17 include files (was ~2600 lines in one file for v16,
  now main asm.asm is ~338 lines)
- New macros added: ROL16, ROR16, TST16, LDAX16, STAX16
- ELSE_SEEN_ARRAY at $0680 for conditional assembly tracking
- LABEL_TYPE variable and constants (LABEL_TYPE_GLOBAL, LABEL_TYPE_LOCAL,
  LABEL_TYPE_MACRO_LOCAL); LABEL_TYPE_MACRO was removed when macro params
  moved off the hash and onto activation frames
- Note: source does NOT use .ifndef or .else in its own code
